The reports merged into #4471 include two causes. The shared parser read dates month first even for day-first tenants. The booking-v3 date hint told people to enter month first while that form read dates in the tenant's order.

## Engineering update

The [course engineering update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows#engineering-update) records #4471 as closed on 5 October 2026. The parser was **fixed**, with `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The hint was **won't fix** because the booking-v3 form was retired. Retirement does not establish that the hint was corrected.

The corresponding public tickets are [the parser](https://github.com/sonicparke/mega-s01e03/issues/1) and [the hint](https://github.com/sonicparke/mega-s01e03/issues/2).

## Reports by cause

The table shows the 4 October export, before engineering closed #4471. Its ticket ownership labels describe that snapshot. It deduplicates report IDs and classifies reports using each tenant's locale and form, rather than intake's browser-based tag. It also notes reports the desk read as one-day moves. Their text alone does not establish a third cause, and the update does not resolve their individual symptoms.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Queue

This timeline shows reports received and merged through the exported snapshot. It is historical data, not a live queue or evidence of when engineering resolved either cause.

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Triage

Do not merge on subject alone. Look up the tenant and channel, compare the underlying cause, and leave reports without enough evidence unplaced for investigation. The accepted subject-only decision remains a historical record; a replacement decision should be made separately.

